1. Architecture Overview
This application enforces role-based data visibility entirely in the CAP backend. The UI receives only the records it is authorised to display — no client-side filtering is involved.

Layer
Technology
Responsibility
Identity Provider
SAP IAS / Corporate IdP
Authenticates user, issues OIDC token
Auth Middleware
SAP XSUAA
Validates JWT, injects scopes/roles/attributes into request
Routing Layer
SAP Approuter
Handles OAuth flow, forwards JWT to backend
Backend Service
SAP CAP (Node.js)
Role-based query filtering, OData exposure
Database
SAP HANA Cloud (HDI)
Persists Persons entity data
Frontend
SAP Fiori / SAPUI5
Displays filtered data, shows user name from JWT


Security principle: The JWT token issued by XSUAA contains the user's assigned scopes. CAP reads these scopes via req.user.is() and applies a WHERE clause before the query reaches the database. No filtered-out records ever travel over the network.

