⚠️  Important: No-Role Scenario
If a user is assigned neither User1Role nor User2Role, the original implementation returns ALL persons. The corrected service.js (Section 5) adds an explicit else branch that returns an empty result set in this case.


3. Approach Review & Issues Found
The implementation approach is architecturally sound. The following 10 issues were identified and must be addressed before production deployment.

#
Area
Issue
Fix
1
srv/service.js
Both role checks run independently — if a user has neither role, no filter is applied (all data exposed).
Add an else block that returns no data when no matching role is found. Wrap in if / else if / else.
2
srv/service.js
req.query.where() called twice can silently overwrite the first condition depending on CAP version.
Use a single conditional branch: if User1Role → where age>40, else if User2Role → where age<40.
3
srv/service.js
req.user.attr.givenName may be undefined when XSUAA attributes are not mapped.
Add null-safe: (req.user.attr?.givenName ?? req.user.id) + " " + (req.user.attr?.familyName ?? "").
4
srv/service.cds
No @requires annotation — the Persons entity is publicly accessible without any role enforcement at CDS level.
Add @requires: ["User1Role","User2Role"] on the entity projection.
5
xs-security.json
"tenant-mode": "dedicated" is correct for single-tenant; must be "shared" for multi-tenant SaaS.
Confirm tenant model. For a single app, dedicated is correct — document this decision explicitly.
6
UI Controller
fetch("/personservice/...") uses a hard-coded relative path. In BTP, the service path depends on approuter mapping.
Use a manifest.json-based OData model or read the service root from environment config.
7
UI Controller
No error handling on the fetch call — if the request fails, "Loading user..." remains permanently.
Add .catch() to display a fallback message or retry.
8
mta.yaml (missing)
No mta.yaml is shown — deployment will fail without it defining CAP module, XSUAA, HDI container, and approuter.
Create mta.yaml with all 4 modules: approuter, srv, db, xsuaa resource.
9
package.json
"auth":"xsuaa" disables local testing entirely. Switching between local mock and production is not covered.
Use "auth": { "kind": "xsuaa" } with .env / default-env.json for local mock credentials.
10
Data seeding
No sample data provided. The entity will be empty on first deploy.
Add db/data/demo-Persons.csv with 10+ rows covering both age brackets to verify filtering.


